{% comment %}
  Main product section. Two-column layout: media gallery (left/top) and
  a scrollable info column (right/bottom) containing every block a
  merchant configures, all inside the ONE product form this section
  owns. Blocks render via {% content_for 'blocks' %} (this theme's
  established theme-blocks convention — see sections/footer.liquid for
  the sibling pattern) — do NOT reintroduce the older
  {% for block in section.blocks %}{% case block.type %} pattern.

  Gallery in this task is minimal (all media, first active) — Task 3
  adds zoom and sticky-buy-box layout polish. Variant-driven live
  updates (price, sold-out, gallery active image, URL) are Task 2.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="product full-width">
  <div class="product__gallery">
    {% if product.media.size > 0 %}
      {% liquid
        assign first_image_media_id = nil
        for media in product.media
          if media.media_type == 'image' and first_image_media_id == nil
            assign first_image_media_id = media.id
          endif
        endfor
      %}
      {% for media in product.media %}
        {% comment %}
          is-active is only ever given to an IMAGE media item — the
          markup below only ever renders an <img> for media_type ==
          'image', so marking a non-image item (e.g. a future video/3D
          item) active would show a blank active slot. Rich media types
          are out of scope for this plan (see Self-Review Notes); this
          just avoids that specific correctness trap once they land.
        {% endcomment %}
        <div class="product__gallery-item{% if media.id == first_image_media_id %} is-active{% endif %}" data-product-media-id="{{ media.id }}">
          {% if media.media_type == 'image' %}
            <img
              src="{{ media | image_url: width: 1600 }}"
              srcset="{{ media | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w, {{ media | image_url: width: 1600 }} 1600w"
              sizes="(min-width: 750px) 50vw, 100vw"
              width="{{ media.width }}"
              height="{{ media.height }}"
              alt="{{ media.alt | default: product.title | escape }}"
              loading="{% if media.id == first_image_media_id %}eager{% else %}lazy{% endif %}"
              {% if media.id == first_image_media_id %}
                fetchpriority="high"
              {% endif %}
            >
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      {% endfor %}

      {% comment %}
        Thumbnail strip: the main gallery above only ever shows one
        media item (.is-active) with no other way to reach the rest —
        without this, photos not tied to a variant's featured_media are
        completely unreachable (spec §5.1). Clicking a thumbnail does
        the same is-active class toggle that a variant change does via
        assets/product-variant-picker.js's updateGalleryImage /
        setActiveGalleryItem (reusing the same data-product-media-id
        hook, not a second parallel mechanism) — only triggered by
        direct user choice instead of a variant match. Only image media
        get a thumbnail since only image media render visible content
        in the main gallery above (see comment on media.media_type
        check there).
      {% endcomment %}
      {% if product.media.size > 1 %}
        <div class="product__gallery-thumbnails" data-product-gallery-thumbnails>
          {% for media in product.media %}
            {% if media.media_type == 'image' %}
              <button
                type="button"
                class="product__gallery-thumbnail{% if media.id == first_image_media_id %} is-active{% endif %}"
                data-product-gallery-thumbnail
                data-product-media-id="{{ media.id }}"
                aria-label="{{ 'product.view_image' | t: index: forloop.index | escape }}"
              >
                <img
                  src="{{ media | image_url: width: 160 }}"
                  alt=""
                  width="80"
                  height="80"
                  loading="lazy"
                >
              </button>
            {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      {% endif %}
    {% else %}
      <div class="product__gallery-item is-active product__gallery-item--placeholder"></div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  <div class="product__info">
    {% form 'product', product, data-add-to-cart-form: true %}
      {% content_for 'blocks' %}
      {% comment %}
        {{ form | payment_button }} must be called here, not inside
        blocks/buy-buttons.liquid — the form tag's block-scoped `form`
        variable does not stay in scope across the content_for 'blocks'
        boundary into a theme-block file (verified live: it silently
        renders empty there, and theme-check flags it statically as
        an UndefinedObject).
      {% endcomment %}
      {{ form | payment_button }}
      {% comment %}
        Same form-scope requirement as payment_button above: the
        payment_terms filter needs the product form's `form` object,
        so it has to be called here rather than from inside a
        content_for 'blocks' theme block.
      {% endcomment %}
      {{ form | payment_terms }}
    {% endform %}
    {{ shop | login_button }}
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .product {
    padding-block: var(--space-8);
    padding-inline: var(--space-4);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }
  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .product {
      padding-inline: var(--space-6);
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-8);
      align-items: start;
    }
    .product__gallery {
      /*
        Without a min-height here, this column is only as tall as its
        own content — one active image plus a thumbnail row, often
        shorter than the info column once a real description is
        present. Since .product__info's sticky "travel range" is
        bounded by how much taller this grid ROW is than info's own
        (viewport-capped) height, a short gallery leaves almost no room
        for the sticky buy-box to actually stay pinned: it stops
        sticking after a few dozen pixels of scroll and then visually
        slides underneath the sticky header for the rest of the page —
        confirmed live, not a theoretical concern (a first attempt at
        this fix used a min-height that came out slightly SHORTER than
        .product__info's own max-height below — arithmetically the
        opposite of what's needed, since the sticky travel range is
        `row height − info's own height`, and a shorter gallery still
        yields ~zero room. This formula intentionally exceeds info's
        max-height by an extra 50vh, live-verified against real
        scrolling, not just computed on paper.)

        Description text scrolls INSIDE .product__info's own
        overflow-y:auto box (it does not push info's rendered height
        past its max-height cap), so this buffer only needs to cover
        realistic scroll distance while the buy box is meant to stay
        visible — it does not need to match an unbounded description
        length.
      */
      min-height: calc(100svh - var(--sticky-header-height, calc(var(--space-8) + var(--space-2))) - var(--space-4) + 100vh);
      /* flex-start, not center: the min-height above is a scroll-buffer
         for the sticky buy-box, not a box the gallery content should be
         vertically centered inside -- centering it here pushes the
         first image roughly halfway down the tall column instead of
         flush with the top of the page like every other product theme. */
      justify-content: flex-start;
    }
    .product__info {
      /*
        top is NOT a hardcoded pixel/rem guess. sections/header.liquid's
        sticky group (.shopify-section-group-header-group:has(header.
        header), top: 0, z-index: 10) is a separate sticky element that
        stays pinned to the viewport for the whole page scroll, and its
        rendered height isn't fixed: it shrinks when initStickyHeader
        toggles .header--condensed during scroll (padding-block changes
        from var(--space-4) to var(--space-2)), which changes the
        wrapper's rendered height. A static estimate would only be
        correct for whichever of those two states it happened to be
        tuned against.

        Instead, sections/header.liquid measures the pinned group's real
        height with a ResizeObserver and publishes it as
        --sticky-header-height on :root (see its javascript block,
        initStickyHeaderHeightVar). That keeps this offset correct
        through the condense/expand transition. The
        calc(var(--space-8) + var(--space-2)) fallback only applies
        before that JS has run its first measurement (e.g. first paint,
        or JS disabled) — it's the same conservative worst-case-header
        estimate used before this was made dynamic, not a value this
        rule relies on in the steady state.
      */
      position: sticky;
      top: calc(var(--sticky-header-height, calc(var(--space-8) + var(--space-2))) + var(--space-4));
      align-self: start;
      max-height: calc(100svh - var(--sticky-header-height, calc(var(--space-8) + var(--space-2))) - var(--space-4) - var(--space-4));
      overflow-y: auto;
    }
  }
  .product__gallery {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .product__gallery-item {
    display: none;
  }
  .product__gallery-item.is-active {
    display: block;
  }
  .product__gallery-item img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .product__gallery-item--placeholder {
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    background-color: var(--color-background-alt);
  }
  .product__gallery-thumbnails {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .product__gallery-thumbnail {
    display: block;
    width: 4rem;
    min-width: 24px;
    min-height: 24px;
    padding: 0;
    /*
      --color-border on --color-background measures ~1.3:1, well under
      the 3:1 non-text-UI contrast threshold (see I5 in the fix-round-1
      review). This is a new component added by this same fix round, so
      it's scoped to --color-foreground-muted (~5.23:1) from the start
      rather than shipping a fresh instance of the same failing pairing.
    */
    border: 1px solid var(--color-foreground-muted);
    background: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    line-height: 0;
  }
  .product__gallery-thumbnail.is-active {
    border-color: var(--color-foreground);
    border-width: 2px;
  }
  .product__gallery-thumbnail img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .product__info {
    /*
      display:flex/gap here used to be applied directly to this element,
      but its only direct child is the form rendered further down this
      file (the form Liquid tag that wraps content_for 'blocks') — all
      8 blocks render as children of that form, not as direct children
      of .product__info. A flex `gap` only applies between direct
      children, so with exactly one child it did nothing: every block
      rendered flush against the next with zero spacing. The flex/gap
      responsibility now lives on `.product__info > form` below, where
      the blocks are the actual flex children; .product__info itself
      keeps only the sticky/scroll layout properties set above.
    */
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .product__info > form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:general.product",
  "blocks": [{ "type": "@theme" }, { "type": "@app" }],
  "settings": [],
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "footer"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
